# Allowlist for scripts/ci/no-private-refs.sh — a security decision, not a convenience.
#
# One rule per line, `path/glob:pattern  # justification`. The glob matches the repo-relative
# path; the pattern is an ERE matched against the whole `git grep` hit (`path:line:text`).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. A justification is mandatory in review.
#
# ⛔ Do NOT add an entry to keep a real internal hostname, address or private repository path
# in a public tree. Remove it instead. An entry is only for a string that *looks* private but
# is not: a documented loopback example, a placeholder, or a term that collides with a rule.
#
# Everything below is a SECURITY RULE that must name `.internal` / service DNS / CGNAT to block
# it, plus the fixtures that assert the block — the guard is searching for the strings the
# feature exists to reject. Each rule is scoped to the file where that is true.

crates/carebus-api/src/netguard.rs:\.internal|\.svc\.cluster\.local|100\.   # the SSRF block rule and the fixtures that assert it
crates/carebus-api/src/routes/llm_providers.rs:\.internal|\.svc\.cluster\.local|100\.   # the provider base_url rule (doc comment) and fixtures asserting refusal
crates/carebus-api/tests/it/llm_providers.rs:\.internal|\.svc\.cluster\.local|100\.   # fixtures asserting a private provider URL is refused
crates/carebus-api/tests/it/source_test_connection.rs:\.internal|100\.   # fixtures asserting a private source URL is refused
web/src/lib/api/providers.ts:\.internal   # client-side mirror of the netguard rule and its message
web/tests/unit/providers.test.ts:\.internal|\.svc\.cluster\.local|100\.   # fixtures asserting the client refuses a private host
